+# UC-28 Move folder design
+
+## Intent and authorized workflow
+
+Implement issue29/UC28 main+AF01..06, FR-FD07/08 and BR07: a current owner changes the parent of a visible active folder to a same-account visible destination or explicit null, without a cycle or unintended selected-scope expansion. The move affects inherited access to its active subtree and contained records, so resulting profile/collection scope and required current native recipient envelopes must be recalculated for every active affected member. Preserve encrypted content, identity, direct links, ownership, client edit times and independent trash/terminal branches. System Requirements authorization/lifecycle matrices, current UC21/23–27 organization/locking/typed identity and future release gates bind the design.
+
+This is an architectural Domain/Command/store/HTTP addition in the authorized all-open-issues batch. Automatic written design/plan self-checks and inline test-first tasks replace repeated human gates; ordinary one fresh whole-branch review, fresh unfiltered six-family coverage, audits/native contracts/exact-head CI and normal develop delivery remain mandatory. Independent formal security/protocol/external-client approval remains development-only deferred. The design was prepared outside the prior checkout, then verified against freshly loaded UC28 specifications after actual UC27 delivery. New checkout baseline equals the tested6110/green-CI merged tree; final fresh current suite remains mandatory.
+
+## Alternatives and selected architecture
+
+An unguarded root parent UPDATE can authorize a stale destination or widen access to descendants; reject it. Reusing RecordMoveStore once per contained record invents parent changes and cannot move a folder atomically; reject it. Use a dedicated FolderMoveStore with current folder-only root admission, an explicit complete active subtree inventory, simulated current/result paths and per-member effective sets, stable ordered locks, current native result evidence and one guarded root parent UPDATE plus distinct old/new immediate parent metadata bumps. No schema, dependency, crypto algorithm, new usable key or server decryption.
+
+## Public boundary
+
+PUT `/api/folders/{id}/parent` requires canonical lowercase dashed nonzero folder UUID, current Heimdall identity, exactly one canonical vault-access header, no query and bounded strict UTF8 JSON/VaultProofBody/no-store. Exactly two required fields: expectedRevision positive safe integer<=9007199254740991 and parentFolderId, explicitly nullable. Omission of parentFolderId rejects400; nonnull value must be canonical lowercase/nonzero. Self-parent rejects400 validation_failed. No encrypted envelope/edit time/profiles/collections/owner/key/cascade overrides.
+
+200 folder_moved returns exactly folderId/parentFolderId/revision/serverSequence. parentFolderId is always serialized, including null. Root revision expected+1 and safe strictly greater server sequence; no envelope or internal IDs. A current same-parent/null-to-null request succeeds and advances only the root. Lost-success retry with old revision returns409; no duplication or stale overwrite.
+
+Missing identity401 authentication_required; missing handle401 vault_access_required; malformed visible input/self-parent/visible descendant destination400 validation_failed; denied current session/selection or native-visible foreign source403 vault_access_denied; hidden/absent/trashed/terminal source or destination/ancestry and selected expansion404 not_found. Relevant active stored ancestry cycle/necessary metadata/native dependency corruption503 persistence_unavailable; stale root, changed inventory/native evidence or exhausted changed counters/sequences409 revision_conflict. Caller cancellation propagates; internal cancellation/supported database/time/JSON/format exceptions503 without private error details. Shared actual empty413 and OpenAPI requiredness/413 metadata remain release followups.
+
+## Current owner root and destination authority
+
+Use current folder PF/CF-only root authority from FolderTrashStore/FolderUpdateStore: target-first candidate<=1, complete active nonterminal same-owner self/upward path to a null-parent root, current statement-time actor/account/session/policy/generation/selected-profile lifecycle. Selected profile is never cleared or widened. A selected owner may act through direct PF ancestry or selected owned CF ancestry. Record-only PR/CR visibility never admits a containing folder. A native RO/RW foreign folder route only establishes visible403 after all relevant contributors pass binding, with one pin parse per party; no foreign resource lock or owned ciphertext inspection before denial. Hidden404 precedes stale/destination/cipher probing; unrelated native/ancestry corruption is ignored.
+
+Nonnull destination must be owned by the same active actor account, active/nonterminal with complete valid ancestry and independently currently visible in the selected folder scope; account-wide access admits any such owned destination. Null is an account-root move. Destination may be the current parent. An otherwise visible self/active descendant destination is invalid400 before root mutation; hidden destination remains404 without a topology oracle. A corrupt relevant stored cycle is503. Source admission resolves before destination and stale metadata for nonowners.
+
+## Per-member resulting sharing and native envelopes (AF06)
+
+Capture active nonterminal same-owner folders rooted at source and active records in those folders. Independently trashed items remain outside active scope with unchanged parent/deadline/operation/snapshots; terminal identities stay typed and reserved. Compute complete before and simulated after ancestry for each folder/record, overriding only the source root's parent to the validated destination. Every member retains its existing internal path below the source. Detect any active simulated cycle before a write.
+
+For each typed member, effective owned collections are active nonterminal direct CF on its folder self/ancestors plus, for records, direct CR. Effective active owned profiles are direct PF on folder self/ancestors plus direct PR for records and PC membership of effective collections. Include direct associations inside the moved subtree so its own routes survive a parent change; inherited old ancestors can disappear and destination ancestors can appear. Typed folder and record IDs must never conflate. With selected access, EACH member's after collection set AND profile set must be a subset of its own before set; reject404 even when the destination is visible but introduces another profile/collection to a descendant. Account-wide access may intentionally expand sharing.
+
+All current active nonterminal grants from resulting owned collections to active recipient accounts contribute required native result evidence, including direct contained-record routes and overlapping grants. Validate owner/recipient pin metadata, exact immutable owner/collection/grant/recipient binding, current collection epoch/grant revision and supported native envelope for every required grant. Cache each exact current pin bundle once. Missing/malformed stored envelope/pins is503 without mutation; removed/inactive/unrelated grants do not contribute. Final root guard compares freshly recomputed native evidence to the verified snapshot and rejects changed/unheld evidence409, never reusing stale pins.
+
+Native immutable content contexts bind owner/kind/publicID/epoch rather than parent. Existing valid native collection recipient envelopes and all content bytes are retained; this boundary cannot fabricate usable keys or prove client authenticated decryption. No new envelope input is added by this endpoint. Actual native tests prove required-binding failure and changed recipient visibility; additional client provisioning and independent client/protocol qualification remain before-release requirements. Effective active server GET/list routes recalculate immediately through new ancestry. Durable inherited visibility events/recipient offline removal delivery belong to UC48, not the current list's immutable snapshot or sequence pagination guarantee.
+
+## Locking and captured inventory
+
+Own account FOR UPDATE first, then own session FOR UPDATE, serializes current owned create/move/trash/association/rotation and implicit new-entity account FK inserts. Admit the current root and resolve the proposed destination before capturing subtree, direct links, current/result per-member sets, needed own active profile/collection metadata, result grants/native evidence and original root/old/new immediate parents. Inventory ordering is stable by kind/publicID/typed keys. Capture opaque member bytes/client times/revisions/sequences/topology so actual recipient edits or growth cannot silently change the admitted set while waiting.
+
+Lock selected own profile FOR NO KEY UPDATE when present; ordered current/result own collections FOR NO KEY UPDATE; ordered result grants FOR SHARE; sorted union of captured subtree folders plus distinct old/new immediate parent folders FOR UPDATE; captured records FOR UPDATE; stored typed links targeting captured folders/records in deterministic order FOR UPDATE. Collections-before-content aligns recipient FolderUpdate/RecordUpdate and UC27. Strong own-account order serializes current same-owner leaf-to-root writers and reciprocal/cycle moves. No foreign account/profile, unrelated content or upward ancestor chain locks. New own entities wait on account FK; existing captured-folder/record FK associations wait on UPDATE locks. Future grant creation remains subject to mandatory BEFOREUC35 implicit recipient-FK audit.
+
+Recompute root/destination/current selection authority after each potentially waiting phase, giving denial before stale metadata. Reload complete subtree/links/per-member before/result scope/needed native evidence after locks. Reject uncaptured child/record/link or changed contributor/metadata409 instead of ignoring it or locking a new earlier resource after content. Final root guard repeats current authority, active same-owner ancestry/destination/cycle/subset conditions and complete captured inventory/native evidence with database statement time. Ordinary current owner writers preserve this contract; future/out-of-band topology writers must be separately audited.
+
+## Atomic structural writes
+
+Validate target supported stored envelope, safe positive member/root counters and UTC representable microsecond client timestamps; no admitted active member has a purge deadline. Preserve descendant opaque bytes without decryption. Validate every distinct immediate parent being bumped for current active/nonterminal state, safe counters/time and absent purge deadline. Exhausted changed parent/root revisions409; no-op skips parent validation/bumping since no parent changes. Hidden authority errors precede these checks.
+
+Guard the root against expected revision/original parent/envelope/sequence/metadata plus complete current move/native/captured scope, set parent to validated destination/null and advance root revision/server sequence/stamp exactly once. Guard miss rechecks current source/destination error before409. Verify exact root identity/owner/parent/result counters, unchanged envelope/clienttime/active lifecycle before proceeding.
+
+If parent changed, bump each distinct old/new immediate parent once with original counters/current lifecycle and verify safe strictly increased sequence; preserve their bytes/time/keys/ownership/other links. Root cannot be an admitted parent. All descendant folder/record bytes/times/topology/revisions, profiles/collections/direct links/native grants/protection/access/trash/queue and recipient metadata remain unchanged. No ancestor structural bump is invented. Target+parent writes commit once or roll back together for guards/faults/cancellation; global sequence gaps may remain. Current statement-time final guarded root write is the authorization boundary; natural expiry after it does not cancel an already authorized atomic structural change.
+
+## Verification and gates
+
+Task1 strict contract/nullable input/output/trusted context and safe result mapping, genuine missing-type RED then focused/whole CommandGREEN. Task2 actual PostgreSQL root/deep mixed subtree/current PF/CF scopes and wide native sharing effects, complete per-member selected subsets with new inherited scopes, descendant/direct-record overlap, and descendant-only required native contributors, self/descendant/inactive/corrupt-cycle targets, all current authority/typed terminal cases, actual native RO/RW denial/record-only read first/no private ancestry leak, missing/overlapping required result envelopes/pins, exact immutable bytes/links and parentbumps/no-op/exhaustion. Real previous RecordTrash/FolderTrash excludes independent items/deadlines. Capture existing-row topology/link growth before content lock; actual owner create/RecordMove/ProfileAssociation/FolderTrash/rotation serialization and recipient FolderUpdate/RecordUpdate races twoorders, reciprocal root moves/cycle attempts and every phase expiry/finalguard evidence change. Natural PostgreSQL faults after target/between parent updates and bad sequences roll back complete graph/retry; outage/internal versus caller cancellation. Actual EXPLAIN root1/bounded active subtree/current-result paths with unrelated folders and exact captured lock set, no foreign account/profile/upward chain locks.
+
+Task3 actual HTTP POST folder/record/profiles and native Master/PerProfile selection + owned collections/foreign grants, strict PUTparent missing-route RED before endpoint/3DI, exact nullable four-field output, full deep-subtree selected subset/sharing key bindings/current GET/list changes/independent trash, transport/currentidentity/allAF01..06. README UC28Done/M03 20 / 26; move/security/operations/release-limit docs and OpenAPIwrite+drift+shape/retainedfolder routes. Lockedrestore/NuGet/nativeOSV153/corpus322x4/helpers36+23/specs/rangewhitespace, final fresh unfiltered6families/all6>=90line/aggregatebranch reporting, sole fullbranchreview/everydeclinedruling+cost/Minors/exact-headCI/normaldevelopdelivery/allnineDoD/ownhashverifiedarchive. No formal/client release approval claim or future durable sync/physical purge completion claim.
+
+Test derivation: With unchanged active PF/CF ancestry, every member inherits the moved root before and after. A destination-inherited scope missing from a descendant is therefore also missing from the root; unchanged direct PR/CR/PF/CF/PC routes do not introduce a move-only scope. The store nevertheless computes both subsets separately for each typed member. Tests exercise real expansion/overlap/preserved direct routes and necessary native grants applying only to descendants, rather than claiming an impossible stable root-subset/descendant-expansion fixture. The Task2 ruling records this limitation for the sole fresh review.
